      <text x="120" y="232" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1A3A6B" font-size="10" font-weight="600">Trained Model</text>
      <text x="120" y="248" text-anchor="middle" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">model.pkl</text>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <h3>Incremental Reproduction</h3>

  <p>Suppose your raw data gets updated. You run <code>dvc repro</code>. DVC detects that the raw data changed, so the prepare stage must rerun. After prepare completes, DVC checks if the output changed. If it did, featurize and train also run. If the processed data is identical to before (perhaps you only changed one row), featurize and train can be skipped.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Bash</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Reproduce entire pipeline (only runs changed stages)</span>
<span class="va">dvc repro</span>

<span class="cm"># Reproduce specific stage and its dependents</span>
<span class="va">dvc repro</span> <span class="st">train</span>

<span class="cm"># View pipeline structure</span>
<span class="va">dvc dag</span>

<span class="cm"># See what would change if you ran repro</span>
<span class="va">dvc status</span>

<span class="cm"># View differences in outputs between versions</span>
<span class="va">dvc plots diff</span> <span class="st">metrics.json</span></code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening here:</strong> <code>dvc repro</code> runs the entire pipeline, but only executes stages whose dependencies changed. <code>dvc dag</code> visualizes the dependency graph. <code>dvc status</code> checks what needs recomputation without running anything. <code>dvc plots</code> compares metrics across pipeline versions, crucial for understanding how changes affect model performance.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- KEY TAKEAWAY -->
  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>DVC pipelines define reproducible ML workflows as code (dvc.yaml)</li>
      <li>Each stage specifies inputs (deps), outputs (outs), and the command to run</li>
      <li><code>dvc repro</code> automatically executes only stages with changed dependencies</li>
      <li>DAG visualization helps understand data flow and catch circular dependencies</li>
      <li>Perfect for multi-week experiments: rerun pipelines and get identical results</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

