<!-- ===== SECTION 3: PRACTICAL SETUP ===== -->
<section class="section reveal" id="dvc-setup">
  <span class="section-label">Implementation</span>
  <h2>Setting Up DVC in Your Project</h2>

  <p>DVC integrates seamlessly with Git. You initialize it like Git, configure a remote backend for data, and commit DVC metadata to Git. Your teammates clone the repository and run two commands to get all data and reproduce your pipelines. It's that simple.</p>

  <p>The setup process follows this pattern: initialize DVC, configure remote storage (where your data will live), track files with <code>dvc add</code>, define pipelines in <code>dvc.yaml</code>, and push everything to Git. Your team members then pull the repository and use <code>dvc pull</code> to download data.</p>

  <h3>Step-by-Step Setup</h3>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Bash</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Step 1: Initialize DVC in your Git repository</span>
<span class="va">cd</span> <span class="st">~/my-ml-project</span>
<span class="va">git init</span>
<span class="va">dvc init</span>              <span class="cm"># Creates .dvc folder with DVC configuration</span>

<span class="cm"># Step 2: Configure remote storage (S3 in this example)</span>
<span class="va">dvc remote add</span> <span class="op">-</span><span class="va">d</span> <span class="va">myremote</span> <span class="st">s3://my-bucket/dvc-storage</span>
<span class="cm"># Alternative: local storage</span>
<span class="cm"># dvc remote add -d local /mnt/dvc-storage</span>

<span class="cm"># Step 3: Add large files to DVC tracking</span>
<span class="va">dvc add</span> <span class="st">data/raw/customers.csv</span>
<span class="va">dvc add</span> <span class="st">data/raw/transactions.csv</span>

<span class="cm"># Step 4: Commit DVC metadata to Git (not the data itself)</span>
<span class="va">git add</span> <span class="st">data/raw/*.csv.dvc data/.gitignore .dvc</span>
<span class="va">git commit</span> <span class="st">-m "Initialize DVC and track raw data"</span>

<span class="cm"># Step 5: Push data to remote storage</span>
<span class="va">dvc push</span>

<span class="cm"># Step 6: Colleagues can now get everything</span>
<span class="va">git clone</span> <span class="st">https://github.com/yourrepo.git</span>
<span class="va">dvc pull</span>                  <span class="cm"># Downloads all data from remote</span></code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening here:</strong> We initialize DVC, set up a remote backend where data will be stored, tell DVC to track large CSV files, commit the metadata files to Git, and push the actual data to the remote backend. When teammates clone the repo, they get the metadata and can pull the data. This workflow is identical to Git push/pull but for data.</p>
  </div>

