<!-- ===== SECTION 4: ADVANCED FEATURES ===== -->
<section class="section reveal" id="dvc-advanced">
  <span class="section-label">Advanced Concepts</span>
  <h2>Advanced DVC Features: Metrics, Plots, and Experiments</h2>

  <p>Beyond versioning and pipelines, DVC integrates with experiment tracking and visualization. You can track metrics alongside data, visualize how model performance changes across pipeline versions, and run parameter sweeps with automatic tracking.</p>

  <h3>Tracking Metrics</h3>

  <p>Add metrics to your pipeline to track model performance automatically. DVC stores metrics with each pipeline run, allowing you to compare performance across versions. This is invaluable for understanding how data changes affect model quality.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">YAML</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># dvc.yaml with metrics tracking</span>
<span class="va">stages</span>:
  <span class="va">train</span>:
    <span class="va">cmd</span>: <span class="st">python scripts/train.py</span>
    <span class="va">deps</span>:
      <span class="op">-</span> <span class="st">data/features/features.csv</span>
    <span class="va">outs</span>:
      <span class="op">-</span> <span class="st">models/model.pkl</span>
    <span class="va">metrics</span>:
      <span class="op">-</span> <span class="st">metrics.json</span>:
          <span class="va">cache</span>: <span class="kw">false</span>  <span class="cm"># Don't cache metrics, always report</span>

<span class="cm"># params.yaml - Track hyperparameters</span>
<span class="va">train</span>:
  <span class="va">learning_rate</span>: <span class="nm">0.001</span>
  <span class="va">batch_size</span>: <span class="nm">32</span>
  <span class="va">epochs</span>: <span class="nm">100</span></code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening here:</strong> We specify metrics output in dvc.yaml and create a params.yaml file for hyperparameters. DVC tracks both automatically. When you change a hyperparameter and rerun the pipeline, metrics are captured alongside the new parameter values. This enables easy comparison of how hyperparameter changes affect model performance.</p>
  </div>

